<article class="passkey-page">
  <header class="project-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">Account</p>
    <h1>Add a security key or passkey</h1>
    <p class="note">
      Give this key a name you will recognize, then follow the browser prompt. You can add more
      than one key, and a second key is strongly recommended.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div
    id="passkey-ceremony"
    data-passkeys
    data-mode="register"
    data-options-json={@options_json}
    data-endpoint="/account/security/keys"
  >
    <form data-passkey-form class="passkey-form">
      <label for="passkey-label">Name this key</label>
      <input
        id="passkey-label"
        name="label"
        type="text"
        value="Security key"
        maxlength="60"
        autocomplete="off"
        required
      />
      <button data-passkey-submit type="submit" class="admin-button button-primary">
        Add security key or passkey
      </button>
    </form>
    <p data-passkey-status class="passkey-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  </div>

  <section class="callout" aria-labelledby="before-heading">
    <h2 id="before-heading">Before you start</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Using a security key?</strong>
      Plug it in (or hold it to your phone), then touch it when it blinks. If it asks for a PIN,
      enter your security-key PIN.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>Using a phone passkey?</strong>
      Choose <strong>Use a phone</strong> in the browser prompt and scan the QR code with your
      camera.
    </p>
    <p>
      A security key with no free passkey slots cannot store another credential. Remove an old
      passkey with your key's management app or use another key.
    </p>
  </section>

  <p class="note"><a class="button-link" href="/account/security">Cancel and go back</a></p>
  <script src="/assets/js/passkeys.js" defer></script>
</article>
